{"The change stops initializing conditional passkeys when no user is selected. Previously, the webauthn context was set up specifically for the null user case, so passwordless UI could still appear on username/password errors. Now it only runs when a user is already selected, which can prevent passkeys from being offered in the username-first flow. Need to restore the original condition or broaden isConditionalPasskeysEnabled to cover the null-user case.": 0.5295066833496094, "Function shouldShowWebAuthnAuthenticators duplicates existing code from WebAuthnAuthenticator.java shouldDisplayAuthenticators (100% similarity). WebAuthnPasswordlessAuthenticator also overrides shouldDisplayAuthenticators (returning false) and is NOT updated in this PR, leaving a parallel/dead override in the hierarchy. The PR should also rename/remove shouldDisplayAuthenticators in WebAuthnPasswordlessAuthenticator to avoid confusion.": 0.09684935212135315, "Function setupReauthenticationInUsernamePasswordFormError duplicates existing code from AbstractUsernameFormAuthenticator.java badPasswordHandler (92% similarity). Should refactor badPasswordHandler to call AuthenticatorUtils.setupReauthenticationInUsernamePasswordFormError(context) instead of its inline equivalent block.": 0.033807165920734406, "Function setPasswordlessPolicyForExternalKey duplicates existing code from PasskeysUsernameFormTest.java passwordLoginWithExternalKey (97% similarity). Should promote setPasswordlessPolicyForExternalKey to the shared base class AbstractWebAuthnVirtualTest so all test classes can use it and eliminate repeated policy setup boilerplate.": 0.04044153541326523}